WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:16.278
"Let us out!" Zann pounded on the door.

2
00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:20.691
"You can't hold us prisoner—we didn't do anything wrong!"

3
00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:24.268
Zing sensed the frustration in his master's voice.

4
00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:27.908
Leaping forward, the dragon tried to burn a hole in the door.

5
00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:31.227
Suddenly—zap! Zing disappeared!

6
00:00:31.228 --> 00:00:34.841
"No!" Darb cried. "What happened to Zing?"

7
00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:39.423
"It's okay," Yog called from out in the hallway. "I'll look after him."

8
00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:42.561
"Let us out!" Gliss cried.

9
00:00:42.562 --> 00:00:46.422
The only answer was the sound of footsteps hurrying away.

10
00:00:46.423 --> 00:00:50.828
Perda kicked the door. "This is horrible!" she exclaimed.

11
00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:56.816
"I know." Zann clenched his fists. "I say we test that Shield spell.

12
00:00:56.817 --> 00:01:01.921
I bet if we all focus our energy together, we can beat the spell."

13
00:01:01.922 --> 00:01:10.649
"No!" Gliss looked alarmed. "If we use magic, Morb will know exactly where we are! He got into the palace before."

14
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:17.389
Darb nodded. "Besides, that Shield spell was probably installed by skilled Magic Masters."

15
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:23.446
"And we're just a bunch of kids," Perda added. "It's not worth the risk."

16
00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:28.095
Zann frowned, ready to argue, but he realized his friends were right.

17
00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:33.444
"Okay," he said. "But zapping can't be the only way to get out of a room.

18
00:01:33.445 --> 00:01:36.832
Let's see if we can figure out another way to escape."

19
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:43.130
"What's the point?" Gliss sighed. "Like Perda said, we're just a bunch of kids.

20
00:01:43.131 --> 00:01:46.922
We can't possibly beat someone as powerful as Morb."

21
00:01:46.923 --> 00:01:50.840
"We can't do anything while we're trapped in here," Zann said.

22
00:01:50.841 --> 00:01:55.961
"If the people at the palace don't want to help us, we need to find someone who will.

23
00:01:55.962 --> 00:02:03.703
I still remember where a few of Boz's powerful Magic Master friends live, including his best friend, Teplo.

24
00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:08.086
Maybe some of them have managed to avoid being caught by the trolls.

25
00:02:08.087 --> 00:02:14.032
If we find Boz's friends and tell them what we've learned, they might know what to do."

26
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:18.420
Perda looked hopeful. "That sounds like a good plan," she said.

27
00:02:18.421 --> 00:02:22.756
"It's too bad that Slib took Boz's diary though. We might need it."

28
00:02:22.757 --> 00:02:26.742
Zann shrugged. "I remember most of what was in there.

29
00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:29.484
Come on. Let's figure out how to escape."

30
00:02:29.485 --> 00:02:32.899
The kids spent the next few minutes searching for an exit.

31
00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:39.186
First they tested the main door. But it was thick, solid wood, and the lock was strong.

32
00:02:39.187 --> 00:02:43.919
There were only two other doors in the room, and they just led to the bedrooms.

33
00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.021
The windows behind the elegant curtains were crisscrossed with strong iron bars.

34
00:02:49.022 --> 00:02:52.182
And the air vents were too small to offer escape.

35
00:02:52.183 --> 00:02:56.559
"It's no use," Perda said at last. "We're trapped."

36
00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:02.037
Gliss collapsed onto a velvet sofa. "At least we're trapped in a nice place.

37
00:03:02.038 --> 00:03:07.937
Probably a lot nicer than wherever Morb is keeping his prisoners."

38
00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:13.834
Morb waved a hand to light another torch on the wall of the large, gloomy underground room.

39
00:03:13.835 --> 00:03:17.897
It was dark, and the ancient texts were difficult to read.

40
00:03:17.898 --> 00:03:23.071
He leaned closer to the dusty old book, studying the scrawled lines on the page.

41
00:03:23.072 --> 00:03:31.999
Then he glanced across the room at his newest contraption: a menacing creation built of bones, wire, and other various objects.

42
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.654
It hadn't been easy to get some of those things, even with his new power.

43
00:03:36.655 --> 00:03:39.639
But the magical device was almost ready.

44
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:47.627
A few more items, a touch of magical energy, and all of Magica would be forced to bow before him.

45
00:03:47.628 --> 00:03:51.197
Hearing footsteps, he turned. The old woman had arrived.

46
00:03:51.198 --> 00:03:56.291
Morb's amber eyes went immediately to the large, lumpy sack she was holding.

47
00:03:56.292 --> 00:04:02.344
"You're late. Are those the paralyzer pythons from Fardark?"

48
00:04:02.345 --> 00:04:06.332
"Yes." She lifted the writhing, hissing sack.

49
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:10.268
"Acquiring them involved great trouble and risk."

50
00:04:10.269 --> 00:04:14.643
"Give them to me," he ordered, striding forward and grabbing the sack.

51
00:04:14.644 --> 00:04:20.155
She stared at him. "What need do you have for such creatures?" she asked.

52
00:04:20.156 --> 00:04:23.850
"Their magic is unpredictable and can be deadly."

53
00:04:23.851 --> 00:04:28.708
"Don't question me." Morb tossed the sack into a corner.

54
00:04:28.709 --> 00:04:32.641
He would add the pythons to his contraption after the woman left.

55
00:04:32.642 --> 00:04:38.997
He didn't want anyone else to know how the thing was constructed, least of all an old busybody like her.

56
00:04:38.998 --> 00:04:43.423
She was still frowning. "I've done all you asked of me," she said.

57
00:04:43.424 --> 00:04:49.469
"My debt to you is repaid twice over. This will be the last time I help you."

58
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:56.676
"Not so fast," Morb said. "I still need a few things that only you can get."

59
00:04:56.677 --> 00:05:02.843
Glaring at him, she stretched to her full height. "And if I refuse?"

60
00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:10.885
Morb shrugged. "If you refuse, I will be forced to tell everyone your unpleasant secrets." He smirked.

61
00:05:10.886 --> 00:05:16.384
"Besides, if you wish to remain in Magica, you shouldn't anger me, Wyssa.

62
00:05:16.385 --> 00:05:19.979
My power grows with every passing day."

63
00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.732
To demonstrate, he touched his fingers lightly together.

64
00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:31.116
Sparks flew everywhere from the slight friction, bouncing off the walls and turning the room into a fireworks display.

65
00:05:31.117 --> 00:05:35.069
The old woman ducked as a spark lit her skirt on fire.

66
00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:38.648
Morb smiled as he felt energy surge through him.

67
00:05:38.649 --> 00:05:44.252
Capturing Boz and some of the other Magic Masters had given him a taste of true power.

68
00:05:44.253 --> 00:05:48.376
The king and queen had increased his strength even more.

69
00:05:48.377 --> 00:05:55.093
"Impressive display, Morb." The old woman calmly touched the flames on her dress to put them out.

70
00:05:55.094 --> 00:06:00.858
"But don't forget that the power you steal through the leeches is temporary."

71
00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:04.188
Morb's eyes shifted toward his contraption.

72
00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:07.810
True, the leeches couldn't keep him strong forever.

73
00:06:07.811 --> 00:06:11.540
But soon he wouldn't need their temporary magic anymore.

74
00:06:11.541 --> 00:06:15.183
Suddenly he couldn't wait to get back to work on his project.

75
00:06:15.184 --> 00:06:18.701
It was time to finish it and seize his destiny.

76
00:06:18.702 --> 00:06:22.657
The trolls would just have to manage without him for the next day or two.

77
00:06:22.658 --> 00:06:33.051
"It is time for you to go, old woman," he told Wyssa. "I have much to do."
